NOBR>Function strings allow you to do neat things,
BOLD>like bold your text...
CLRB>Or clear the terminal.
NOBR>Function strings use one to five characters followed by a greater than sign (>).
They will be found and removed from anywhere in the line.
CLRB>NOBR>Currently implemented:
SPD(0) CLRA, CLRB, BOLD, RED, YLW, GRN, BLU, PNK, PUR, LBLU, LME, WHI, LGRY, GRY, DGRY, BLK, BGRED, BGYLW, BGGRN, BGBLU, BGPNK, BGPUR, BGLME, BGWHI, BGGRY, BGBLK, ITAL, CONT, NOBR, ESC, SPD, PORT, CMT, NMPLT

CLRA and CLRB clear the terminal after/before the line is displayed.

RED, YLW, GRN, BLU, PNK, PUR, LBLU, LME, WHI, LGRY, GRY, DGRY, and BLK change the text color.

BGRED, BGYLW, BGGRN, BGBLU, BGPNK, BGPUR, BGLME, BGWHI, BGGRY, and BGBLK change the background color.

CONT makes the text continue without waiting for input.
NOBR removes the full line between text.
SPD, ITAL, BOLD, PORT, and CMT use parentheses to extract a value.
SPD allows you to set the speed of the text, using a number of seconds to wait after displaying each character.
NOBR>CONT>It would be written like this:
 ESC>SPD(0.1)
NOBR>PORT will add a portrait before the text, like an RPG.
PORT<:3>Like this!
NOBR>ITAL allows you to italicize selections of text.
ITAL(Like this!)
NOBR>BOLD allows you to bold selections of text.
BOLD(Like this!)
Bold and italic can be combined into BOLD(ITAL(Bold Italics!))
CMT is a comment; anything in this tag will be ignored.
ESC makes the line ignore all of these neat functions.
